type: article
title: "Covariogram Uniqueness with One Regular Body in R³: A Candidate Proof via Area Measures and Fourier–Laplace Zeros"
authors:
  - family-names: Comparini
    given-names: Andrea
version: 1.0-candidate
date-released: 2026-10-09
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23250931
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23250931"
repository-code: "https://github.com/andreacomparini/covariogram-uniqueness-candidate"
abstract: >-
  A candidate proof for covariogram uniqueness of a C9 convex body with
  positive Gaussian curvature in R3 among arbitrary convex competitors,
  up to translation and central reflection. The two central propositions
  require independent review. Partial Lean verification of 33 supporting
  and conditional theorems does not certify the complete theorem.
keywords:
  - covariogram
  - convex geometry
  - inverse problems
  - phase retrieval
  - Lean
  - AI-assisted mathematics
